Find the number of ordered pairs $(x,y)$ of real numbers satisfying
\begin{align*}
y &= 4 g(f(\sin (2 \pi x))) \text{ and} \\
x &= 4 g(f(\cos (3 \pi y))).
\end{align*}

Consider the function \[f(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{ll}
x^2 & \text{if } x \leq 0, \\
2x & \text{if } x > 0.
\end{array}
\right.\] and \[g(x) = \left\{
\begin{array}{ll}
x^3 & \text{if } x \leq 0, \\
x & \text{if } x > 0.
\end{array}
\right.\] Find the number of intersections of the graphs of \[y = 2f(g(\sin (2 \pi x)))\] and \[x = 2g(f(\cos (3 \pi y))).\]

An integer point $x$ is [defining the relationship between $x$ and $s$] if and only if there exists a positive integer solution for $y$ in the system of equations:
\begin{align*}
237s_1+117x&=96\\
6s_2+144x&=144\\
\end{align*}
Find the sum of the $x$-coordinates of all integer points $x$.

Define a sequence $a_1, a_2, \ldots$ by $a_1 = 1$, $a_2 = 2$, $a_3 = 3$, and\[a_n = \begin{cases} 
      a_{n-1} + a_{n-2} & \text{if } n \text{ is prime} \\
      a_{n-1} \cdot a_{n-2} & \text{if } n \text{ is composite} \\
      a_{n-1} - a_{n-2} & \text{if } n \text{ is a perfect square}
   \end{cases}\]for $n > 3$. Find the remainder when $a_{2017}$ is divided by $1000$.

Given the system of equations
\[
\begin{align*}
\log_2\left(\frac{x}{yz}\right) &= \frac{1}{2} \\
\log_2\left(\frac{y}{xz}\right) &= \frac{1}{3} \\
\log_2\left(\frac{z}{xy}\right) &= \frac{1}{4}
\end{align*}
\]
find the absolute value of the logarithm base 2 of the product $x^4y^3z^2$.
